\section{Efimov states}
The \emph{Efimov states} were initially proposed in 1970 as hypothetical, stable quantum states of coupled three-body systems \cite{Efimov70} such as three coupled bosons in ultracold `experiments'. A most interesting feature of such ultracold 3-boson systems was the presence of an infinite number of Efimov states when the boson coupling was weak but finite when the coupling became strong. 

Subsequently, in 2006, there have been published claims of experiments indicating the presence of such ``Efimov trimers''. (See also the following references) \cite{Kraemer--etal2k6}.

\begin{thebibliography}{99}

\bibitem{Efimov70}
Vitali Efimov. 1970. Energy levels arising from resonant two--body forces in a three--body system, \emph{Physics Letters B}, Volume 33, Issue 8 , 21 December 1970, Pages 563--564.

\bibitem{Kraemer--etal2k6}
T. Kraemer et al., 2006. Evidence for Efimov quantum states in an ultracold gas of caesium atoms, \emph{Nature}, {\bf 440}, 315--318 (16 March 2006).

\bibitem{EHYG72}
E. Hadjimichael, S. N. Yang, G. E. Brown.,1972.  A model for short range correlation in the three--body system., \emph{Physics Letters B}, Volume 39, Issue 5, 29 May 1972, Pages 594--598.

\bibitem{ZDKC92}
M. V. Zhukov, B. V. Danilin, A. A. Korsheninnikov, L. V. Chulkov. 1992.
Structure of $^6 He$ nucleus as a three--body system: $\alpha$--particle and neutron momentum distributions. \emph{Nuclear Physics A}, Volume 538, 2 March 1992, Pages 375--381.

\bibitem{SFHM2k7}
Y. Suzuki, Y. Fujiwara, W. Horiuchi, H. Matsumura.,2007. M.  Dynamics of macroscopic and microscopic three--body systems., \emph{Nuclear Physics A}, Volume 790, Issues 1--4, 15 June 2007, Pages 223c--228c.

\end{thebibliography}
